# Text is stored LF in this repo, whatever the machine that syncs it uses.
# The mirror is written by a script running on Windows, and a `git archive`
# there converted EVERY text file to CRLF once (0.3.1) — harmless for Kotlin,
# fatal for gradlew: `#!/bin/sh` is not an interpreter, and CI died with
# "cannot execute: required file not found". Normalising on commit means the
# blob is right even when the working tree that produced it was not.
* text=auto
gradlew text eol=lf
gradlew.bat text eol=crlf

# Shell scripts and the bundled bridge CLI MUST stay LF-only. A CR in a
# shebang (`#!/usr/bin/env bash\r`) breaks the script when it runs on the
# user's server / phone. Windows checkouts must never CRLF-convert these,
# or a build from a fresh clone would ship a broken conch-bridge.
*.sh text eol=lf
app/src/main/assets/conch-bridge text eol=lf
